# TailorIT configuration. Copy to `.env` (never commit it). One file feeds both apps; DEPLOY.md explains each part.
# No line here sets a value: a blank KEY= or a commented line means the default. A commented # KEY=value line shows
# that default; to change it, remove the # and set your value. In production keep NODE_ENV unset (npm start sets
# production) or set it to production, never anything else.
# Saved from PowerShell? UTF-16 is fine; the launchers decode it.

# --- Addresses ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every address and port TailorIT uses is set here; change them here and restart (npm run dev, or npm run build then
# npm start: a production build holds the web's way to the API). Blank = the default shown. Values must agree:
# - APP_ORIGIN is the address people open in the browser: http(s)://host:port, no path. The API accepts changes only
#   from pages at this exact address (open TailorIT there, not at another name of the same computer), and Google
#   sign-in must list it as an authorized JavaScript origin. The autofill extension must be built for the same
#   address (its TAILORIT_ORIGIN, then rebuild and reload it).
# - WEB_HOST and WEB_PORT are where the web server listens: localhost (this computer only; http://localhost:3100 and
#   http://127.0.0.1:3100 both work), an address of this computer on your network (such as 192.168.1.20: that
#   network), or 0.0.0.0 (every network interface: your LAN, and beyond if the firewall allows). Unless a reverse
#   proxy is in front, APP_ORIGIN is an address the web server listens on, with port WEB_PORT.
# - API_HOST and API_PORT are where the API listens. The browser never calls it: the web server passes /api on to it,
#   so the API can stay on 127.0.0.1 (this computer only) whatever WEB_HOST is.
# - API_INTERNAL_URL is where the web server reaches the API. Blank = http://API_HOST:API_PORT (127.0.0.1 for
#   localhost, 0.0.0.0 or ::). Set it only when the API runs on another computer, and keep it in step with API_PORT.
# - MCP_PUBLIC_URL is the MCP endpoint's address that Settings > Integrations shows your AI client. Blank =
#   APP_ORIGIN/mcp (v3.1 OAUTH: the web server and your reverse proxy pass /mcp, /oauth/... and /.well-known/oauth-...
#   on to the API, so Claude and ChatGPT connect at the address people open; DEPLOYMENT.md). Set it only when clients
#   reach /mcp somewhere else (such as http://127.0.0.1:4100/mcp, the API itself).
# - MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS: more host names or IP addresses (comma separated, no port) that /mcp answers to. It answers to
#   localhost, 127.0.0.1, API_HOST and MCP_PUBLIC_URL's host already; any other name is refused, which stops a web
#   page from reaching it through a name it controls (DNS rebinding).
# Example, TailorIT on your LAN at 192.168.1.20 with the API private:
#   APP_ORIGIN=http://192.168.1.20:3100
#   WEB_HOST=192.168.1.20
#   WEB_PORT=3100
#   API_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   API_PORT=4100
# SECURITY: a LAN address or 0.0.0.0 in WEB_HOST or API_HOST exposes that server to the network. Sign-in, sessions and
# tokens still apply, but use HTTPS (a reverse proxy) beyond your own network.
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3100
# WEB_HOST=localhost
# WEB_PORT=3100
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# API_PORT=4100
API_INTERNAL_URL=
MCP_PUBLIC_URL=
MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# --- Core -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database, uploads and caches. Default: %LOCALAPPDATA%\TailorIT on Windows, ~/.local/share/tailorit elsewhere.
DATA_DIR=
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Database: PostgreSQL 18 (v30 SCH) ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TailorIT keeps everything in PostgreSQL 18. With DATABASE_URL blank it runs its own server from npm (the embedded
# PostgreSQL; on Windows it needs the Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 Redistributable x64, 14.44 or later): loopback
# only, a random password kept beside its data folder (<PG_DATA_DIR>.password), started by npm run dev and npm start.
# - DATABASE_URL: another PostgreSQL 18 server instead (a managed service), as
#   postgres://user:password@host:5432/database. Blank = the embedded server.
# - PG_PORT: the embedded server's port on 127.0.0.1. Blank = 5442.
# - PG_DATA_DIR: the embedded server's data folder. Blank = the pg folder in DATA_DIR.
# - PG_POOL_MAX: the most connections the API (or a command) opens at once. Blank = 10.
DATABASE_URL=
PG_PORT=
PG_DATA_DIR=
PG_POOL_MAX=

# --- Sign-in (passwordless: Google button + six-digit email code) ---------------------------------------------------
# SESSION_TTL_DAYS=30
# Accounts with these emails become administrators (comma or space separated).
ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Shown as "Contact admin" on the sign-in page (mailto). v2.0: also the address Subscribe and Buy extra credit show
# (the constant ADMIN_CONTACT_EMAIL, which Admin > Constants can change). An email address, or blank for none.
CONTACT_EMAIL=
# Google Identity Services client id (no secret needed).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# SMTP for sign-in codes. Port 465 = implicit TLS.
SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_SECURE=
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=

# --- AI (local Claude CLI, signed in to a subscription; no API key) ------------------------------------------------
# AI_ENABLED=true
# Path or name of the CLI (blank: claude on the PATH).
# AI_CLI_BIN=claude
# AI_CLI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# AI_CLI_EFFORT=low
AI_CLI_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# AI_CLI_CONCURRENCY=4
# AI_CLI_BACKGROUND_SLOTS=1
# The interactive CLI processes one account may run at once (the autofill extension runs two tasks of a form at once);
# empty or 0: AI_CLI_CONCURRENCY (a server of one person keeps every slot). Background work never counts here.
AI_CLI_PER_ACCOUNT=
# AI_CLI_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
# AI_CLI_FIRST_EVENT_MS=30000
# v1.3 C --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Thinking: on (the default) leaves it to the CLI, as before v1.3. off passes the CLI's thinking-off setting on every
# call, so an answer is written without hidden reasoning first, which can cut the output tokens a lot. Try off first
# with Admin > AI's test prompt, once for each model in use: set off, restart, and run the test (it runs on
# AI_CLI_MODEL; for Haiku 5.5, POST /api/admin/ai/test {"model":"claude-haiku-5-5"} as an administrator, or set
# AI_CLI_MODEL to it for one test). Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5 refuse disabled thinking on the API, and only a real call
# shows what the CLI sends. If a test fails with a 400 about thinking, keep on.
# AI_CLI_THINKING=on
# A model per AI task. The tasks whose answer is a closed choice or an extraction that TailorIT checks run on Haiku 5.5
# (claude-haiku-5-5) unless set here: AUTOFILL_CLASSIFY, AUTOFILL_PICK, RESUME_ANALYSIS and JOB_ANALYSIS (v2.0: and
# JOB_SEARCH and CUSTOM_FILTER). Every other task runs on AI_CLI_MODEL. Which model a task runs on: its
# AI_MODEL_<TASK> below when set, else that default, else AI_CLI_MODEL; so setting AI_CLI_MODEL alone keeps those on
# Haiku. To put a task back on Sonnet, name it:
#   AI_MODEL_JOB_ANALYSIS=claude-sonnet-5-5
# One model for every task: set all of them (AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_CLASSIFY, AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_PICK,
# AI_MODEL_RESUME_ANALYSIS, AI_MODEL_JOB_ANALYSIS, AI_MODEL_JOB_SEARCH, AI_MODEL_CUSTOM_FILTER) to the AI_CLI_MODEL
# value. Admin > AI shows the model of each task; Admin > AI usage what each task used over the last 1, 7 and 30 days.
# end v1.3 C ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-feature overrides (empty = the task's default model, see above, and AI_CLI_EFFORT).
AI_MODEL_RESUME_IMPORT=
AI_MODEL_BULLETS=
AI_MODEL_JOB_ANALYSIS=
AI_MODEL_COVER_LETTER=
AI_MODEL_TEMPLATE_FILL=
AI_MODEL_RESUME_ANALYSIS=
# The autofill extension's AI steps: the tiebreak between a field's options, what an unusual question asks, (from
# Phase 6) a draft for a free-text question, and (from v2) an answer to a question the profile does not settle.
AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_PICK=
AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_CLASSIFY=
AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_DRAFT=
AI_MODEL_AUTOFILL_ANSWER=
# v1.4 D: tailoring a resume and its cover letter (empty = AI_CLI_MODEL; tailoring is meant for Sonnet 5.5).
AI_MODEL_TAILOR=
# end v1.4 D
# v2.0: AI job search (a sentence to the classic search's filters) and the Custom filter of Prepare & Queue (Haiku 5.5
# unless set).
AI_MODEL_JOB_SEARCH=
AI_MODEL_CUSTOM_FILTER=
AI_EFFORT_RESUME_IMPORT=
AI_EFFORT_BULLETS=
AI_EFFORT_JOB_ANALYSIS=
AI_EFFORT_COVER_LETTER=
AI_EFFORT_TEMPLATE_FILL=
AI_EFFORT_RESUME_ANALYSIS=
AI_EFFORT_AUTOFILL_PICK=
AI_EFFORT_AUTOFILL_CLASSIFY=
AI_EFFORT_AUTOFILL_DRAFT=
AI_EFFORT_AUTOFILL_ANSWER=
# v1.4 D
AI_EFFORT_TAILOR=
# end v1.4 D
AI_EFFORT_JOB_SEARCH=
AI_EFFORT_CUSTOM_FILTER=
# When Claude refines job analyses (the rule-based analysis always comes first, at once): ingest (the default) = every
# added job, once, newest first, through a background backlog (jobs from before the upgrade go last; opening or saving
# a job never queues one); saved = saved jobs only; lazy = the first time a job is opened; off = rules only.
# AI_JOB_ANALYSIS=ingest
# Background AI analyses per hour for popular jobs (lazy mode only; 0 = off).
# AI_JOB_ANALYSIS_WARMUP_PER_HOUR=0
# auto = Claude also reads each uploaded resume, once, after its quick rule-based reading (the file itself is never
# changed); off = the rule-based reading only.
# AI_RESUME_ANALYSIS=auto
# The most tasks the job and resume backlogs start per hour (0 = no cap). Background AI work also waits while AI is
# paused or the Claude usage window is nearly used up, so people's own AI requests keep their room.
# AI_JOB_ANALYSIS_PER_HOUR=0
# AI_RESUME_ANALYSIS_PER_HOUR=20

# --- Rendering and files --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chrome/Edge for PDF export (blank = auto-detect an installed Chrome/Edge).
CHROME_PATH=
# PDF_RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# PDF_MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
# UPLOAD_MAX_MB: the largest upload, now a constant (the v3.0 block below; still read from .env at start).

# --- Job ingestion --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ingest worker (`npm run dev` and `npm start` start it beside the API; v30 S1-API) reads each enabled source when
# it is due: every 6 hours to 7 days by its cadence tier, one request at a time per host.
# false: no source is read on a schedule (Admin > Sources > Run now still reads one).
# INGEST_ENABLED=true
# INGEST_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Identify yourself to job boards (include a contact address).
# INGEST_USER_AGENT=TailorIT job ingest (contact: admin@example.com)
# free_tailor's Job Data Lake, opened read-only: the path of its free_tailor.db. Blank: none (a lake source may name its
# own path in Admin > Sources).
FT_LAKE_DB_PATH=
# FT_LAKE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=45
# Google Sheet import (Admin > Import jobs: a one-time, read-only import of one tab; nothing is written to Google):
# the JSON key of a Google Cloud service account with the Google Sheets API turned on. Share each sheet with the
# key's client_email as a Viewer. Blank = service-account-key.json in the repository root (git-ignored; never commit
# a key). A relative path is read from the repository root. Write Windows paths without quotes.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_FILE=

# --- New outside reads: TailorIT's bot identity and the services' keys (v30 SCH) -------------------------------------
# v3.0's new kinds of outside read (board discovery, the new job sources, USAJOBS, Himalayas and Jobicy, Wikidata, SEC
# and GLEIF lookups, company websites and career pages, logo.dev) say who they are with one User-Agent, and every one
# of them stays off until it names TailorIT's public bot page (what it reads, how often, how to opt out) and a role
# mailbox, never a person's address. Today's job ingestion keeps INGEST_USER_AGENT above.
#   BOT_USER_AGENT=TailorIT/1.0 (+https://<public site>/bot; <role mailbox>)
# Blank, or still holding <...> or an example address = off. A value that is not one line of plain text starting with
# TailorIT/ and naming the page and the mailbox stops the API at start, naming the key. `npm run doctor` shows it.
BOT_USER_AGENT=
# The services' keys (each source or step stays off while its key is blank): USAJOBS (developer.usajobs.gov; its
# requests also carry the mailbox above), Himalayas, and logo.dev (a paid plan). Never commit a key.
USAJOBS_API_KEY=
HIMALAYAS_API_KEY=
# v30 E2: logo.dev's secret key (sk_...): TailorIT asks its server API for a logo and keeps a copy; the publishable key
# (pk_, for hot-linking its images) is not used.
LOGO_DEV_KEY=

# --- Autofill extension (TailorIT Autofill) -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The extensions Settings > Autofill hands a connect code to (comma separated). Unset = the id that the extension's
# manifest key fixes for every local build (below); empty = none, so the page shows the code to type in.
# AUTOFILL_EXTENSION_IDS=flmloalhjldmcihejnmkndbcnhaacmng
# How long a connected browser stays connected, counted from when it connected (fixed, never extended).
# AUTOFILL_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS=90
# How long the extension's AI requests wait for Claude before answering "still working" (the extension then asks again
# every 1.5 s), in milliseconds: 0 to 20000, since the extension gives up on any request at 25 s. Blank = 10000.
AUTOFILL_AI_WAIT_MS=

# --- v2.0: the central constants -------------------------------------------------
# Every business limit, budget, price, window and term, and every limit or status message people see. Each value is an
# administrator's override (Admin > Constants, kept in the database), else the value set here, else the default shown.
# Uncomment a line to set it here; an empty value counts as unset. A value that does not parse stops the API at start,
# naming the key and the form it takes. Limits take a whole number or "unlimited"; money is dollars with at most 6
# decimal places ("0.10"); true/false/1/0; AI_PRICES is JSON. Budgets, prices and the capacity values are never shown
# to people. ADMIN_CONTACT_EMAIL is read from CONTACT_EMAIL (Sign-in, above). v1.5's PREBUILD_PER_HOUR is still read
# for PREPARE_PER_HOUR.
# -- Accounts and plans --
# How many jobs the extension may auto-apply to for a Free account in each auto-apply window.
# FREE_AUTO_APPLY_PER_DAY=7
# How many jobs the extension may auto-apply to for a Paid account in each auto-apply window.
# PAID_AUTO_APPLY_PER_DAY=unlimited
# What TailorIT's AI may spend for a Free account each day before extra credit is used. People never see it.
# FREE_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=0.10
# What TailorIT's AI may spend for a Paid account each day before extra credit is used. People never see it.
# PAID_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=0.50
# How many resumes of every kind a Free account may hold. At the limit, new resumes and edits are blocked.
# FREE_RESUME_LIMIT=30
# How many resumes of every kind a Paid account may hold. The safety cap applies as well.
# PAID_RESUME_LIMIT=unlimited
# Whether a Free account may use AI job search. Classic search is always available.
# FREE_AI_JOB_SEARCH=false
# Whether a Paid account may use AI job search. Classic search is always available.
# PAID_AI_JOB_SEARCH=true
# Whether a Free account's own AI may connect to TailorIT's MCP server.
# FREE_MCP=true
# Whether a Paid account's own AI may connect to TailorIT's MCP server.
# PAID_MCP=true
# One Paid term. "Extend" adds one term to the later of now and the current end.
# PAID_TERM=P1M
# Admin > Users marks a Paid term that ends within this many days, and its "Paid ending" filter lists them.
# PAID_ENDING_DAYS=7
# Whether a Free account may download several resumes at once as a ZIP.
# FREE_BATCH_DOWNLOAD=false
# Whether a Paid account may download several resumes at once as a ZIP.
# PAID_BATCH_DOWNLOAD=true
# -- Server AI (never shown to people) --
# The share of the server's Claude usage at which every server-AI action is refused.
# SERVER_AI_BLOCK_THRESHOLD=0.98
# What TailorIT's own spend estimate counts as full when the CLI reports no usage. Unlimited: no fallback.
# SERVER_AI_CAPACITY_USD_PER_WINDOW=unlimited
# The hours TailorIT's own spend estimate sums over.
# SERVER_AI_CAPACITY_WINDOW_HOURS=5
# How long a usage reading with no reset time keeps counting.
# SERVER_AI_READING_TTL_MINUTES=300
# USD per million tokens by model, used only when the CLI reports no cost. "*" prices any other model.
# AI_PRICES={"claude-opus-5-5":{"input":4,"output":20,"cacheRead":0.2,"cacheWrite":5},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"input":2,"output":10,"cacheRead":0.1,"cacheWrite":2.5},"claude-haiku-5-5":{"input":0.1,"output":0.5,"cacheRead":0.01,"cacheWrite":0.125},"*":{"input":4,"output":20,"cacheRead":0.2,"cacheWrite":5}}
# -- Auto-apply and the queue --
# The length of the window the auto-apply limits count in. 1 counts per day.
# AUTO_APPLY_WINDOW_DAYS=1
# The day windows of more than one day are counted from. Set here only (Admin > Constants cannot change it).
# AUTO_APPLY_WINDOW_EPOCH=2026-01-01
# The most rows an account's auto-apply queue holds.
# QUEUE_SIZE_MAX=500
# -- Resumes --
# A technical cap on resumes for every account, Paid included. It is not a plan limit.
# RESUME_SAFETY_CAP=5100
# Tailorings one account may start in an hour (Tailor my resume, the extension's tailor, an own-AI tailor).
# TAILOR_PER_HOUR=10
# The most resumes one batch download ZIP holds.
# BATCH_DOWNLOAD_MAX_RESUMES=100
# -- Prepare & Queue --
# Server Prepares started per account per hour. It paces the runner and refuses nothing. Also read from
# PREBUILD_PER_HOUR.
# PREPARE_PER_HOUR=30
# The most saved jobs one Prepare & Queue takes.
# PREPARE_BATCH_MAX=100
# A Prepare left waiting for the person's own AI this long is cancelled.
# PREPARE_MCP_STALE_DAYS=7
# "required": a letter only when the application requires one. "always": a letter for every job.
# COVER_LETTER_MODE_DEFAULT=required
# The longest Custom filter prompt a person may save.
# CUSTOM_FILTER_PROMPT_MAX_CHARS=1000
# Jobs one Custom filter AI call judges.
# CUSTOM_FILTER_BATCH=10
# Years of experience a posting may ask above the person's before the qualification filter fails.
# QUALIFICATION_YEARS_GRACE=1
# "saved": jobs in some Saved Jobs, oldest saved first. "all": every active job. "off": none.
# JOB_ANALYSIS_V2_REREAD=saved
# "default": the default resume as it is. "similar": the most similar existing resume. "tailor": a new tailored resume
# for each job.
# PREPARE_RESUME_MODE_DEFAULT=tailor
# -- Jobs and search --
# The most jobs one Save all saves (was SAVE_ALL_LIMIT).
# SAVE_BATCH_MAX=100
# The longest sentence AI job search takes.
# AI_SEARCH_TEXT_MAX_CHARS=300
# -- MCP (your own AI) --
# Live MCP tokens one account may hold (was MAX_MCP_TOKENS).
# MCP_TOKENS_PER_ACCOUNT=10
# Calls one MCP token may make a minute.
# MCP_CALLS_PER_MINUTE=120
# Calls one MCP token may make an hour.
# MCP_CALLS_PER_HOUR=2000
# The longest custom instructions text. Tied to the database column's check, so it is set in .env only.
# MCP_CUSTOM_INSTRUCTIONS_MAX_CHARS=4000
# Job ids one filter_jobs answer holds.
# MCP_FILTER_PAGE_MAX=500
# -- The day --
# When the AI budget and the auto-apply counter reset each day. Changing this moves today's reset at once.
# DAY_RESET_TIME=00:00
# The time zone of the daily reset. Changing this moves today's reset at once.
# DAY_RESET_TIME_ZONE=America/Los_Angeles
# How messages name the reset time zone, as in "12:00 AM Pacific Time".
# DAY_RESET_ZONE_LABEL=Pacific Time
# -- Announcements --
# Announcement banners shown at once, the most severe first.
# ANNOUNCEMENTS_SHOWN_MAX=3
# -- Housekeeping: how long rows are kept --
# Days of per-person AI spend kept for the admin.
# AI_SPEND_KEEP_DAYS=400
# Days finished Prepares are kept. Each application's newest is always kept.
# PREPARE_KEEP_DAYS=90
# Days a Custom filter verdict is kept before the job is judged again.
# CUSTOM_FILTER_VERDICT_KEEP_DAYS=30
# Days settled auto-apply reservations are kept. Only the current window is counted.
# RESERVATION_KEEP_DAYS=35
# Days after its expiry before an announcement is deleted.
# ANNOUNCEMENT_KEEP_DAYS=90
# Days the prepared answers of a job taken out of Saved Jobs, and never applied to, are kept.
# DRAFT_ANSWERS_KEEP_DAYS_UNSAVED=90
# Messages people see ({placeholders} are filled in; write a line break as \n)
# MSG_BATCH_DOWNLOAD_PAID=Downloading several resumes at once is available with a Paid account. Subscribe to unlock it.
# MSG_PREPARE_NO_RESUME=Add a resume first: Prepare & Queue needs a default resume or one to choose from.
# LABEL_RESUME_MODE_DEFAULT=Only my default resume
# LABEL_RESUME_MODE_SIMILAR=Use my best-matched resume
# LABEL_RESUME_MODE_TAILOR=Always tailor
# MSG_AI_UNAVAILABLE=AI is currently unavailable. Your account may be flagged, or the server's AI may not be working. Please contact the admin or use your own AI via MCP.
# MSG_AI_USAGE_EXHAUSTED=You've used your AI usage. Get extra credit or use your own AI via MCP.
# MSG_LIMIT_AUTO_APPLY=You've reached the Free account limit of {limit} auto-applies per day. Your limit resets at {reset_time}. Subscribe for unlimited auto-apply.
# MSG_LIMIT_RESUMES=You've reached the Free account limit of {limit} saved resumes. Delete some resumes or subscribe for unlimited storage.
# MSG_PAID_AI_SEARCH=AI job search is available with a Paid account. You can keep using classic search, or subscribe to unlock AI search.
# MSG_SUBSCRIBE_CONTACT=Please contact the admin to subscribe.
# MSG_CREDIT_CONTACT=Please contact the admin to purchase extra credit.
# MSG_CONTACT_EMAIL_MISSING=The admin has not set a contact email yet.
# MSG_PREPARE_CONFIRM=This can use a significant amount of your AI usage. Continue?
# MSG_PREPARE_CONFIRM_DONT_SHOW=Don't show this again
# MSG_AUTO_APPLY_USAGE={used} of {limit} used today
# MSG_WAITING_FOR_RESET=Daily auto-apply limit reached. These jobs wait until {reset_time}.
# MSG_FILTERED=Filtered: {reason}
# MSG_PREPARE_NOT_SAVED=This job is no longer at Saved in your Job Tracker, so it was not prepared.
# MSG_PREPARE_NO_JOB=This Tracker entry has no job posting in TailorIT, so it cannot be prepared.
# MSG_PREPARE_ACTIVE=This job is being prepared already.
# MSG_PREPARE_ALREADY_QUEUED=This job is in your auto-apply queue already.
# MSG_PREPARE_QUEUE_FULL=Your auto-apply queue is full ({limit} jobs). Clear finished jobs, then Prepare & Queue again.
# MSG_PREPARE_INTERRUPTED=The TailorIT update interrupted this preparation. Prepare & Queue it again.
# MSG_PREPARE_NEEDS_COPY=Your resume is an uploaded file with no editable copy yet. Make an editable copy in Documents, then Prepare & Queue again.
# MSG_PREPARE_RESUME_FAILED=The tailored resume could not be made.
# MSG_PREPARE_LETTER_FAILED=The cover letter could not be written.
# MSG_PREPARE_ANSWERS_FAILED=Some answers could not be prepared; they are made during the application instead.
# MSG_PREPARE_TOOK_TOO_LONG=The AI took too long to answer.
# MSG_PREPARE_FAILED=Something went wrong while this job was prepared.
# MSG_DIRECT_QUEUE_REMOVED=Jobs are queued by Prepare & Queue. Save the job, then Prepare & Queue it on the Auto-apply page.
# MSG_CUSTOM_FILTER_PENDING=The custom filter has not judged this job yet.
# MSG_MANUAL_ONLY=This job is applied to by hand. Open it from TailorIT's Auto-apply page.
# MSG_LIMIT_AUTO_APPLY_ACCOUNT=You've reached your account's limit of {limit} auto-applies per day. Your limit resets at {reset_time}.
# MSG_LIMIT_RESUMES_ACCOUNT=You've reached your account's limit of {limit} saved resumes. Delete some resumes to add new ones.
# MSG_PREPARE_BATCH_MAX=Choose at most {max} saved jobs.
# MSG_BATCH_DOWNLOAD_MAX=One download holds up to {max} resumes. Select fewer and try again.
# MSG_TEXT_TOO_LONG=Use at most {max} characters.
# MSG_AI_SEARCH_TIMEOUT=The AI search took too long. Try again, or use the classic search.
# MSG_AI_SEARCH_FAILED=The AI search did not finish. Try again, or use the classic search.
# MSG_CUSTOM_FILTER_FAILED=The custom filter could not judge these jobs.
# MSG_TAILOR_PER_HOUR=You have tailored {max} {max|resume|resumes} in the last hour, the most TailorIT starts in an hour. Please wait {minutes} {minutes|minute|minutes} and try again.
# MSG_MCP_OFF=Connecting your own AI to TailorIT's MCP server is not available for your account.
# MSG_MCP_TOKENS_MAX=This account already has {max} MCP tokens, the most TailorIT allows. Revoke one you no longer use, then make a new one.
