# v3.1 NOTIFY: in-app notifications (docs/design/v3.1/24-notifications-usage.md): how long they are kept, when extra
# credit counts as low, and the words of each kind. Each is also editable in Admin › Constants.
# NOTIFICATIONS_KEEP_DAYS=90
# CREDIT_LOW_USD=1.00
# MSG_NOTIFY_PREPARE_FINISHED_TITLE={ready} {ready|application|applications} ready to review
# MSG_NOTIFY_PREPARE_FINISHED_BODY=TailorIT prepared {ready|it|them}. Check {ready|it|them} in your queue on Auto-apply.
# MSG_NOTIFY_PREPARE_SOME_FAILED=TailorIT couldn't prepare {failed} more: open Auto-apply to try again.
# MSG_NOTIFY_PREPARE_FAILED_TITLE=TailorIT couldn't prepare {failed} {failed|application|applications}
# MSG_NOTIFY_PREPARE_FAILED_BODY=Open Auto-apply to see what went wrong and try again.
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_SUBMITTED_TITLE=Applied: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_SUBMITTED_BODY=Your browser extension sent this application.
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_NEEDS_YOU_TITLE={title} at {company} needs you
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_NEEDS_YOU_BODY=The extension stopped before sending it. Open Auto-apply to finish the application yourself.
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_FAILED_TITLE=Couldn't apply to {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_AUTO_APPLY_FAILED_BODY=Open Auto-apply to see what happened, then apply another way.
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_VERIFIED_TITLE=Job verified: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_VERIFIED_BODY=TailorIT read the posting and it is open. Everyone can find this job now.
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_WAITING_TITLE=Waiting for approval: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_WAITING_BODY=TailorIT read the posting. Only you can see this job until an admin approves it.
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_UNVERIFIED_TITLE=Couldn't verify {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_UNVERIFIED_BODY=TailorIT couldn't read the posting, so only you can see this job. Open it and choose Retry read to try again.
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_REFUSED_TITLE=Not added: {title} at {company}
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_REFUSED_UNNAMED_TITLE=TailorIT didn't add the job you linked
# MSG_NOTIFY_JOB_REFUSED_BODY=TailorIT won't list this posting.
# MSG_NOTIFY_AI_DAY_USED_TITLE=You've used today's AI budget
# MSG_NOTIFY_AI_DAY_USED_BODY=TailorIT now uses your extra credit ({credit} left) until your budget starts again at {reset_time}.
# MSG_NOTIFY_AI_DAY_USED_NO_CREDIT=New AI work waits until your budget starts again at {reset_time}. Buy extra credit in Settings › Account to keep going.
# MSG_NOTIFY_CREDIT_LOW_TITLE=Your extra credit is low
# MSG_NOTIFY_CREDIT_LOW_BODY={credit} left. Buy more in Settings › Account so TailorIT can keep working past your daily budget.
# MSG_NOTIFY_CREDIT_USED_UP_TITLE=You've used all your extra credit
# MSG_NOTIFY_CREDIT_USED_UP_BODY=New AI work waits for your daily budget, which starts again at {reset_time}. Buy more credit in Settings › Account.
# MSG_NOTIFY_PAID_ENDING_TITLE=Your Paid plan ends in {days} {days|day|days}
# MSG_NOTIFY_PAID_ENDING_BODY=It ends on {date}, and your account then moves to Free. See Settings › Account to keep Paid.
# MSG_NOTIFY_EXTENSION_DISCONNECTED_TITLE=Your browser extension is disconnected
# MSG_NOTIFY_EXTENSION_DISCONNECTED_BODY={browser} no longer works with TailorIT. Connect it again in Settings › Autofill to keep auto-applying.
# MSG_NOTIFY_EXTENSION_EXPIRED_BODY={browser}'s connection ran out. Connect it again in Settings › Autofill to keep auto-applying.
# MSG_NOTIFY_EXTENSION_UNNAMED=Your browser
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_REVIEW_TITLE={count} new {count|item|items} in Review
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_REVIEW_BODY={pending} {pending|item waits|items wait} for a decision in Admin › Review.
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUN_FAILED_TITLE=A run of {source} failed
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUN_FAILED_BODY=See its log in Admin › Runs. TailorIT tells you once an hour at most: runs that fail after it are listed there too.
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_SOURCE_DISABLED_TITLE=TailorIT turned off {source}
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_SOURCE_DISABLED_BODY=It failed {failures} {failures|time|times} in a row. Check it in Admin › Sources, then turn it on again. Sources turned off later this hour are listed there too.
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUNS_PAUSED_TITLE={admin} paused {what}
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUNS_CONTINUED_TITLE={admin} continued {what}
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUNS_BODY=See Admin › Runs for what runs now.
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUNS_ALL=every run
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_RUNS_SOURCE={source}'s runs
# MSG_NOTIFY_ADMIN_SOMEONE=An admin
# end v3.1 NOTIFY
# v31 RUNS: admins pause and continue job-source runs (Admin › Runs, Admin › Sources). RUN_STOP_POLL_MS is .env only:
# how often the API and the ingest worker look whether an admin paused one of their runs (it stops within about this).
# RUN_STOP_POLL_MS=5000
# MSG_INGEST_RUNS_PAUSED=Runs are paused, so no source runs now. Continue the runs in Admin › Runs first.
# MSG_INGEST_SOURCE_PAUSED=This source is paused. Continue it first, then run it.
# MSG_INGEST_SOURCE_NEVER_PAUSED=This kind of source is never run, so there is nothing to pause.
# MSG_INGEST_RUN_NOT_RUNNING=This run has already finished, so there is nothing to pause. Refresh the list to see how it ended.
# MSG_INGEST_RUN_NOT_PAUSED=Only a paused run can be continued. To read this source again, use Run now in Admin › Sources.
# end v31 RUNS
# v31 OAUTH: Claude and ChatGPT connect through TailorIT's OAuth 2.1 server (docs/design/v3.1/23-mcp-oauth.md). The
# client document's size and read time are .env only.
# OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_MINUTES=60
# OAUTH_REFRESH_IDLE_DAYS=30
# OAUTH_CODE_SECONDS=120
# OAUTH_REQUEST_MINUTES=10
# OAUTH_GRANTS_PER_ACCOUNT=20
# OAUTH_REGISTRATIONS_PER_HOUR=100
# OAUTH_CALLS_PER_MINUTE=120
# OAUTH_TOKEN_CALLS_PER_MINUTE=60
# OAUTH_CIMD_FETCHES_PER_MINUTE=10
# OAUTH_CIMD_MAX_BYTES=10000
# OAUTH_CIMD_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# OAUTH_CIMD_CACHE_MINUTES=60
# OAUTH_RECORD_KEEP_DAYS=7
# MSG_OAUTH_REQUEST_GONE=This connection request has ended or was already answered. Go back to your AI app and connect TailorIT again.
# MSG_OAUTH_GRANTS_MAX=You have {max} connected AI {max|app|apps}, the most TailorIT allows. Disconnect one in Integrations, then connect again.
# MSG_OAUTH_RATE_LIMIT=There have been too many connection requests.
# v31 FIX-AUTH: the two per-address budgets above (registrations, client documents) sit under ceilings for all callers
# together; a client document that failed waits before another read; a refresh token sent again within the grace gets
# a new pair (an app that retries after a lost answer stays connected).
# OAUTH_REGISTRATIONS_PER_HOUR_ALL=2000
# OAUTH_CIMD_FETCHES_PER_MINUTE_ALL=60
# OAUTH_CIMD_FAILURE_MINUTES=5
# OAUTH_REFRESH_REUSE_GRACE_SECONDS=60
# end v31 FIX-AUTH
# end v31 OAUTH
# v31 LINK: every job comes from its link (docs/design/v3.1/21-jobs-from-links.md): the add pipeline's switches,
# limits and words.
# ADD_JOB_PAGE_READ=true
# NEW_JOBS_ADMIN_APPROVAL=false
# JOB_ADDS_PER_HOUR=30
# ADMIN_ADD_LINKS_MAX=1000
# JOB_LINK_QUEUE_KEEP_DAYS=30
# MSG_JOB_ADD_PUBLISHED=TailorIT read this posting from its link and added it to Jobs.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_WAITING=TailorIT read this posting from its link. It is in your saved jobs now, and everyone sees it once an admin approves it.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_PRIVATE=TailorIT couldn't read this posting from its link, so only you can see this job until TailorIT verifies it.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_NEEDS_DETAILS=TailorIT couldn't read this posting from its link. Add the job's title and company to save it for yourself: only you will see it.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_REFUSED_CLOSED=This posting has closed, so TailorIT did not add it.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_REFUSED_LINK=TailorIT can't add this link. Paste the job posting's own web address (https://...).
# MSG_JOB_ADDS_RATE_LIMITED=You added {limit} jobs by link in the last hour. Wait {minutes} more {minutes|minute|minutes}, then try again.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_IMPORT_LINKS=TailorIT reads each posting from its link: {queued} {queued|link is|links are} queued for reading, and every other column is ignored.
# MSG_JOB_ADD_TOO_MANY_LINKS=Add at most {max} links at a time.
# MSG_JOB_ONLY_YOU_UNTIL_VERIFIED=Only you can see this job until TailorIT verifies it.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_UNREADABLE_HOST=TailorIT never reads this site (a job board or a sign-in page). Add the job from the employer's own posting to share it.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_NO_POSTING=The page doesn't describe its job in a form TailorIT reads (schema.org JobPosting).
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_ROBOTS=The site's robots.txt asks automated readers not to read this page.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_BLOCKED=The site asked for a sign-in or a check TailorIT does not pass.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_UNAVAILABLE=The site didn't answer. Try again later.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_NOT_SET_UP=TailorIT can't read job pages on this server yet. Your administrator can turn this on. Until then, the job stays yours.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_UNLISTED=The posting is not on its board's public list, so TailorIT cannot read it.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_OPTED_OUT=This company asked TailorIT not to read its site.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_REJECTED=An admin decided this link is not a job TailorIT lists.
# MSG_JOB_REVIEW_PAGE_UNREADABLE=TailorIT couldn't read this page from its link, so it can't be published. Reject it, or try again later.
# MSG_JOB_VERIFY_NOT_YOURS=Only the person who added this job, or an admin, can ask TailorIT to read it again.
# end v31 LINK
